   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to establishing a campaign\nto promote public awareness of the causes of oral disease and its prevention",
    "basePrintNo": "S8348",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8348-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §207-b, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8348\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to establishing a\ncampaign to promote public awareness of the causes of oral disease and\nits prevention\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to raise public awareness about the impor-\ntance of good oral health to good overall health and well-being.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Adds section 207-b of the public health law to direct the\ndepartment of health, in consultation with the department of education,\nto develop and implement a campaign to promote public awareness of the\nimportance of good oral health by utilizing public forums, social media\nand mass media, as well as educational materials and information on the\ndepartment's website, to target high risk groups through local depart-\nments of health and local health care practitioners. § 2 establishes the\neffective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nGood oral health is essential for vital functions of life, including\neating, breathing and speaking. Dental disease can result \"in poor\nnutrition, school absences, missed workdays and increasing public and\nprivate expenditures for dental care.\"' Periodontal disease increases\nthe risk of heart disease, diabetes and premature birth. Dentists are\nimportant front-line health care providers in that infectious diseases,\ncancer, immune disorders, and nutritional deficiencies are often\nreflected in the health of a patient's teeth and gums. This bill will\nprovide for a public awareness campaign to underline the importance of\ndental care and oral hygiene in promoting overall health and well-being.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
